 "contract": "shell-variable-inventory-v1",
 "purpose": "Record which names a shell answers from itself rather than from the environment, so an expansion of one is not lowered into a program that reads an environment variable nobody set.",
 "note": "A generated program resolves a name through the process environment. That is right for `PATH` and wrong for `RANDOM`, which every shell here answers from itself and no environment carries: the generated program reads nothing and produces an empty string where the script produced a number. INHERITED means the name was in the environment this was measured in; SHELL means the shell supplied a value the environment did not; ABSENT means neither. A name marked SHELL anywhere is one the frontend must not lower as an ordinary expansion, whatever it is in the shell being lowered.",
